__pycache__
.livekit-demo/corp-ca.pem

# Measurement data from the two-host teleop latency runs. Both hosts hold
# overlapping-but-different subsets of the same runs; committing them from
# either side produces conflicts in content that cannot be merged.
examples/local_video/scripts/results/
examples/local_video/scripts/results-*/

# The consolidated archive is the same data in buckets, so it is ignored for the
# same reason. Its two index files are not data and are the committed record of
# what every run was.
/results/*
!/results/MANIFEST.csv
!/results/README.md
llvm.sh

# Measurement data stays out of git (operator directive). These trees hold run CSVs,
# logs, generated PDFs and the embedded-PNG report bundle -- tens of MB that would be
# committed by a plain `git add -A`. `results/` above is already covered; these three
# are the archive buckets and the two cross-host exchange directories, which were
# untracked rather than ignored and so were one careless add away from landing in the
# history. Bucket README.md files are documentation, not data, and are kept.
examples/local_video/scripts/archive/**
!examples/local_video/scripts/archive/**/
!examples/local_video/scripts/archive/**/README.md
examples/local_video/scripts/archive-hosta/
examples/local_video/scripts/incoming/
# Measurement data mirrored between hosts. Same reason as results/: both hosts hold
# overlapping-but-different subsets, and committing from either side produces
# unmergeable conflicts. These three were UNTRACKED rather than ignored, so a plain
# `git add -A` from either host would have put 155 MB of run data into the history.
/results-hostb/
/results-shared/*
!/results-shared/README.md
!/results-shared/**/README.md
/teleop-test-matrix/e1-gate-2-samples/
/teleop-test-matrix/incoming/
# Dated campaign trees holding the joint two-host capture: publisher jsonl/CSV, Host B's
# subscriber CSVs and its stored raw I420 frames. The 2026-09-10 tree alone is >7 GB of
# frames. These were UNTRACKED rather than ignored, which is the state that put 155 MB
# into reach of a plain `git add -A` twice before.
/overnight-20??-??-??/
# Modem diag captures. A DLF holds the full baseband log -- IMSI, cell IDs,
# RRC/NAS signalling -- so it must never reach the history. The venv is a
# local install with absolute paths baked in and is useless to anyone else.
/diag-capture/logs/
/diag-capture/venv/
# Random 4 MB upload payload for the controlled uplink probe (S1). Not data, not code.
/diag-capture/up4m.bin
# Runtime flock for the DIAG serial port, created per cell by hop-recorder.sh,
# capture-around-cell.sh and test-qcsuper-build.sh. Zero-byte lock state, not source.
/diag-capture/.ttyUSB0.lock
